</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/5610cb48bdb77a6978937ae5033d6b9574af473d" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:8.066ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle A^{\Omega }\rtimes H}"/></span> is called the <b id="mwUg">base</b> of the wreath product.</p>

<p id="mwUw">The <b id="mwVA">restricted wreath product</b> <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt60" id="mwVQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"A \\text{ wr}_{\\Omega} H"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle A{\text{ wr}}_{\Omega }H}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>A</mi>
        <msub>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mtext> wr</mtext>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="normal">Ω<!-- Ω --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mi>H</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle A{\text{ wr}}_{\Omega }H}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1e355364bba2db03881a8ff105dfaff0995eae40" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:8.396ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle A{\text{ wr}}_{\Omega }H}"/></span> is constructed in the same way as the unrestricted wreath product except that one uses the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Direct_sum_of_groups" title="Direct sum of groups" id="mwVg">direct sum</a> as the base of the wreath product. In this case, the base consists of all sequences in <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt61" id="mwVw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"A^{\\Omega}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle A^{\Omega }}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>A</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="normal">Ω<!-- Ω --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle A^{\Omega }}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/6413fe01c088d830443c0706467e15a9968d5f4e" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:3.162ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle A^{\Omega }}"/></span> with finitely many non-<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Identity_element" title="Identity element" id="mwWA">identity</a> entries.  The two definitions coincide when <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt62" id="mwWQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\Omega"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle \Omega }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi mathvariant="normal">Ω<!-- Ω --></mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \Omega }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/24b0d5ca6f381068d756f6337c08e0af9d1eeb6f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.678ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \Omega }"/></span> is finite.</p>

<p id="mwWg">In the most common case, <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt63" id="mwWw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\Omega = H"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle \Omega =H}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi mathvariant="normal">Ω<!-- Ω --></mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mi>H</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \Omega =H}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/07486e4486f121ba8268c5c82842a4d61699ca43" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:6.84ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \Omega =H}"/></span>, and <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt64" id="mwXA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle H}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>H</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/75a9edddcca2f782014371f75dca39d7e13a9c1b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.064ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H}"/></span> acts on itself by left multiplication. In this case, the unrestricted and restricted wreath product may be denoted by <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt65" id="mwXQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"A \\text{ Wr } H"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle A{\text{ Wr }}H}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>A</mi>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mtext> Wr </mtext>
        </mrow>
        <mi>H</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle A{\text{ Wr }}H}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9eedaa603dd7e270bd2b1e4d57038540126c8f31" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:8.268ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle A{\text{ Wr }}H}"/></span> and <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt66" id="mwXg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"A \\text{ wr } H"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle A{\text{ wr }}H}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>A</mi>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mtext> wr </mtext>
        </mrow>
        <mi>H</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle A{\text{ wr }}H}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/ef7bbb15eaa265277d93599e0c7fe0943c6d104d" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:7.558ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle A{\text{ wr }}H}"/></span> respectively. This is called the <b id="mwXw">regular</b> wreath product.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwYA" aria-labelledby="Notation_and_conventions"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Notation_and_conventions">Notation and conventions</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Wreath_product&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Notation and conventions"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwYQ">The structure of the wreath product of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt67" id="mwYg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"A"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle A}">
  <semantics>
