</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/abc22e9d57becf0ba976a1d5e8a043375daaa899" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:19.637ex; height:3.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle |A\wr _{\Omega }\!H|=|A|^{|\Omega |}|H|}"/></span>.<sup about="#mwt100" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-2" id="mwlA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwlQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlw">]</span></span></a></sup></dd></dl>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwmA" aria-labelledby="Universal_embedding_theorem"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Universal_embedding_theorem">Universal embedding theorem</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Wreath_product&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Universal embedding theorem"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt101" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwmQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Universal embedding theorem"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1368532237" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt102" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt101" id="mwmg">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_embedding_theorem" title="Universal embedding theorem">Universal embedding theorem</a></div>
<p id="mwmw">If <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt103" id="mwnA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"G"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle G}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>G</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle G}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f5f3c8921a3b352de45446a6789b104458c9f90b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.827ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle G}"/></span> is an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Group_extension" title="Group extension" id="mwnQ">extension</a> of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt104" id="mwng" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"A"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle A}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>A</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle A}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7daff47fa58cdfd29dc333def748ff5fa4c923e3" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.743ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle A}"/></span> by <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt105" id="mwnw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle H}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>H</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/75a9edddcca2f782014371f75dca39d7e13a9c1b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.064ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H}"/></span>, then there exists a subgroup of the unrestricted wreath product <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt106" id="mwoA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"A\\wr H"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle A\wr H}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>A</mi>
        <mo>≀<!-- ≀ --></mo>
        <mi>H</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle A\wr H}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/d091a7a2554182db07331301218ab89ea30f7f6b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.505ex; width:5.486ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle A\wr H}"/></span> which is isomorphic to <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt107" id="mwoQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"G"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle G}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>G</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle G}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f5f3c8921a3b352de45446a6789b104458c9f90b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.827ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle G}"/></span>.<sup about="#mwt108" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwog"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpA">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpQ">]</span></span></a></sup> This is also known as the <i id="mwpg">Krasner–Kaloujnine embedding theorem</i>. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krohn–Rhodes_theorem" title="Krohn–Rhodes theorem" class="mw-redirect" id="mwpw">Krohn–Rhodes theorem</a> involves what is basically the semigroup equivalent of this.<sup about="#mwt111" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Meldrum1995_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Meldrum1995"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Meldrum1995-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Meldrum1995-4" id="mwqA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwqQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwrA" aria-labelledby="Canonical_actions_of_wreath_products"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Canonical_actions_of_wreath_products">Canonical actions of wreath products</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Wreath_product&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Canonical actions of wreath products"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwrQ">If the group <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt112" id="mwrg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"A"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle A}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>A</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle A}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7daff47fa58cdfd29dc333def748ff5fa4c923e3" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.743ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle A}"/></span> acts on a set <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt113" id="mwrw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\Lambda"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle \Lambda }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi mathvariant="normal">Λ<!-- Λ --></mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \Lambda }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/0ac0a4a98a414e3480335f9ba652d12571ec6733" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.613ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \Lambda }"/></span> then there are two canonical ways to construct sets from <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt114" id="mwsA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\Omega"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle \Omega }">
