<li id="mwARc">Wreath products arise naturally in the symmetries of complete rooted <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_(data_structure)" title="Tree (data structure)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwARg">trees</a> and their <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graph_(discrete_mathematics)" title="Graph (discrete mathematics)" id="mwARk">graphs</a>. For example, the repeated (iterated) wreath product <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt169" id="mwARo" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"S_2\\wr S_2\\wr\\cdots\\wr S_2"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle S_{2}\wr S_{2}\wr \cdots \wr S_{2}}">
